# [DD-13b.W23.1] A CONTINUATION LINE INDENTED LESS THAN THE BLOCK'S FIRST.
#
# THIS FIXTURE ASSERTS A DEFECT, NOT A PROMISE. The dedent strip is a BYTE
# COUNT, so a line indented less than the first silently LOSES content and
# the file still exits 0 — filed as K57 (docs/dev/known_issues.md), wrong
# under every revision of the design, and deliberately NOT fixed in this
# step: two independent reds must not share a step, and a step whose
# acceptance is the structure layer would then have two unrelated causes
# behind one failure (w23_impl §7.3, manager ruling R4).
#
# `tests/rxtsource/` has no known-fail bucket, so the pin is the
# assertion itself: the check asserts TODAY'S WRONG VALUE, and the day K57
# is fixed this fixture goes RED. That red is the signal to invert it to
# the correct value — the pin cannot outlive the defect silently, because
# the fix breaks it.
description |
    line one at four
  line two at two
    line three at four

pattern a+
m "aaa" 0 3
